 "captions": [
  {
   "start": 2.2,
   "end": 5.961,
   "who": "N",
   "text": "3:07 AM. The agent has been running for nine hours."
  },
  {
   "start": 6.561,
   "end": 9.847,
   "who": "V",
   "text": "Why babysit it? Start it before bed. Check it in the morning."
  },
  {
   "start": 10.447,
   "end": 16.146,
   "who": "N",
   "text": "Nobody told it what done looked like. By sunrise, four thousand lines, built on a wrong premise."
  },
  {
   "start": 18.646,
   "end": 23.576,
   "who": "N",
   "text": "If you work with coding agents, you're already a manager. These are the habits that betray you."
  },
  {
   "start": 25.076,
   "end": 26.365,
   "who": "V",
   "text": "It looks done. Ship it."
  },
  {
   "start": 26.965,
   "end": 31.513,
   "who": "N",
   "text": "Looks done isn't done. Give it a test, a build, a screenshot. Then ask for the proof."
  },
  {
   "start": 32.663,
   "end": 35.417,
   "who": "V",
   "text": "Make the dashboard faster. It'll figure it out."
  },
  {
   "start": 36.017,
   "end": 40.581,
   "who": "N",
   "text": "Skip what the code already says. Give it the goal, the why, the limits, and what done means."
  },
  {
   "start": 41.731,
   "end": 43.721,
   "who": "V",
   "text": "I'll just fix it again. Every session."
  },
  {
   "start": 44.321,
   "end": 48.255,
   "who": "N",
   "text": "Corrected it twice? Write it into Claude dot M D, or make it a skill."
  },
  {
   "start": 49.405,
   "end": 51.375,
   "who": "V",
   "text": "Never! Always! Think harder!"
  },
  {
   "start": 51.975,
   "end": 57.173,
   "who": "N",
   "text": "Over-process is the new micromanagement. Hard rules only for what must never bend."
  },
  {
   "start": 58.323,
   "end": 61.126,
   "who": "V",
   "text": "Five agents, same task. Five times the output!"
  },
  {
   "start": 61.726,
   "end": 67.414,
   "who": "N",
   "text": "No. One merge conflict with five authors. Plan first, and split the work so nothing overlaps."
  },
  {
   "start": 68.564,
   "end": 71.62,
   "who": "V",
   "text": "One more correction. This time it'll work."
  },
  {
   "start": 72.22,
   "end": 77.099,
   "who": "N",
   "text": "Two failed fixes means the problem is upstream. Start fresh, with a better prompt."
  },
  {
   "start": 78.249,
   "end": 80.854,
   "who": "V",
   "text": "Six hundred lines. Tests are green. Approve."
  },
  {
   "start": 81.454,
   "end": 86.115,
   "who": "N",
   "text": "That isn't review. That's ratification. Treat every diff like you'll get paged for it."
  },
  {
   "start": 87.265,
   "end": 88.641,
   "who": "V",
   "text": "It'll stop when it's finished."
  },
  {
   "start": 89.241,
   "end": 95.323,
   "who": "N",
   "text": "Before any unattended run, answer five questions. Done, checks, boundaries, limits, and who signs off."
  },
  {
   "start": 96.473,
   "end": 99.196,
   "who": "V",
   "text": "Forty percent of our code is written by AI!"
  },
  {
   "start": 99.796,
   "end": 105.663,
   "who": "N",
   "text": "That's activity, not quality. Count the reverts. Add agents only as fast as your checks can watch them."
  },
  {
   "start": 106.813,
   "end": 108.618,
   "who": "V",
   "text": "It's cheap. Build everything."
  },
  {
   "start": 109.218,
   "end": 113.57,
   "who": "N",
   "text": "Building is cheap. Reviewing isn't. The question isn't can we. It's should we."
  },
  {
   "start": 114.72,
   "end": 118.474,
   "who": "V",
   "text": "I run five agents. So I can manage five people."
  },
  {
   "start": 119.074,
   "end": 123.412,
   "who": "N",
   "text": "You can't. People are harder. Agents are eager, confident, and all the same."
  },
  {
   "start": 124.562,
   "end": 126.214,
   "who": "V",
   "text": "Just trust the machine."
  },
  {
   "start": 126.814,
   "end": 130.412,
   "who": "N",
   "text": "Make it argue against its own answer. And own every line that ships."
  },
  {
   "start": 131.662,
   "end": 134.754,
   "who": "N",
   "text": "You don't need the title. Be the reason good code gets written."
  }
